export anchor AnatomyChartStyle:
    number: 128
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Anatomy chart
    idea: The dashboard as an antique scientific plate in sepia, where projects are segments of a sectioned specimen with lettered leader lines, numbers are labelled measurements and activity reads as numbered field notes.
    base: light
    palette:
        agedPaper: #e9dcbf, the page around the plate
        plate: #f6edd8, the plate, the figure centre and label discs
        ironGallInk: #33241a, text, outlines and leader lines
        sepia: #5f4730, captions, key details and stipple
        redOchre: #8e3b22, label letters, overdue, the Behind square and focus
        hairline: #b49c78, dotted rules and grid lines, never text
        washes: #d9b98f #b9c4d6 #c4d3b0 #d8b4a6 #cdbfd4 #bccfcf, figure segments a to f
        onTrack: #2f5d34, the ring with a dot
        atRisk: #80500a, the open triangle
    type:
        One stack, Baskerville, Baskerville Old Face, Libre Baskerville,
        Hoefler Text, Garamond, Times New Roman, serif. The greeting is 46px
        400 at 1.1, measurements 52px with old-style numerals, section
        titles 20px small caps tracked 0.14em over a rule, figure captions
        15px small caps then italic, body 17px at 1.55, label letters 20px
        bold italic in red ochre.
    layout:
        A plate up to 1240px with a 1px ink edge doubled 8px outside and a
        soft drop shadow. A centred masthead reads A systematic chart of the
        working week, then BRIGHTWORK in widely spaced caps and with figures
        drawn from life, over a double rule. A ruled bar holds the nav as
        roman numbered small caps links and the tools, a ruled italic search,
        a dark New project button, a round bell and a line drawn avatar with
        the name. The title block has a boxed Plate XXXI, the greeting with
        the date in italic, and an Observation note with a red ochre edge
        saying 4 tasks are overdue. Two columns follow. On the left, Fig. 1
        is a sectioned ring of six segments sized by task count, each in its
        own wash with the completed part hatched outward from the centre,
        170 tasks in all in the middle, and leader lines ending in lettered
        discs a to f. A Key to Fig. 1 lists each letter with the name, team,
        percent, tasks and due date, and the status. On the right, Fig. 2
        shows the four numbers as large numerals over caliper rules with
        lettered italic captions, Fig. 3 is an engraved line chart with a
        stippled area, values on each point and a dashed week divider, and
        Notes from the field is a numbered list of activity. A double rule
        and an italic credit line close the plate. Below 960px the columns
        stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 24px between sections, 40px between columns, 28px plate margins.
    density: Moderate, like a printed plate. One large figure and a key, then smaller figures and notes.
    corners: Square frames and boxes. Round only for label letters, the bell and the figure.
    borders: A 1px ink plate edge doubled 8px out, double rules at top and foot, dotted hairlines between key rows.
    shadows: One soft drop under the plate, as if pinned to a wall. Nothing else.
    icons:
        Engraved line marks at 15px with the small caps word, a ring with a
        dot for On track, an open triangle for At risk and a solid square
        for Behind. Leader lines end in small ink dots.
    focus: A 2px red ochre outline offset 3px.
    tone: Victorian naturalist, such as Plate XXXI, Observation, Notes from the field and drawn from life.
